      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should have a return code, so the host can retry this if TZ got interrupted (by a non-secure interrupt or just yielded).\n\nThe way Trusty currently works (other TEEs might do things differently, I think some of them support yielding direct messages):\n* The VM availability messages are non-yielding direct messages (handled with interrupts disabled). Since it can\u0027t block, the handler just queues up work to be done later (top-half/bottom-half-style).\n* Trusty still needs cycles to do actual work. The direct message is followed by an `FFA_RUN` which _can_ be interrupted, so we need to run it as many times as needed.\n* We poll in between `FFA_RUN` calls to check whether the VM availability message has completed.",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "703e66f0_06921c0c",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 314,
